{"lines": ["How is Hitler connected to Kermit the Frog?", "In nineteen thirty-eight, British prime minister Neville Chamberlain signed the Munich Agreement with Hitler, hoping to avoid war.", "In nineteen forty, Chamberlain's fellow Conservative, Winston Churchill, replaced him as prime minister.", "On Victory in Europe Day, nineteen forty-five, Churchill stood on the palace balcony beside young Princess Elizabeth.", "In two thousand nine, Queen Elizabeth the Second welcomed Barack and Michelle Obama to Buckingham Palace.", "And in twenty fourteen, Michelle Obama introduced Kermit the Frog at a White House screening of Muppets Most Wanted.", "How is Adolf Hitler connected to Grug?", "In October nineteen forty, Hitler met Spain's dictator Francisco Franco at Hendaye, trying to pull Spain into the war.", "Spain stayed out, and in nineteen fifty-nine Franco welcomed President Dwight Eisenhower to Madrid.", "Eisenhower's vice president for eight years was a young senator named Richard Nixon.", "In December nineteen seventy, Elvis Presley showed up at the White House asking President Nixon for a narcotics badge.", "In nineteen sixty-eight, Elvis posed with his newborn daughter, Lisa Marie.", "In two thousand one, Lisa Marie sat beside Nicolas Cage at the Capitol, and the next year they married.", "And Grug, the caveman dad of The Croods, is voiced by Nicolas Cage.", "How is Joseph Stalin connected to Elmo?", "In nineteen forty-five, Joseph Stalin sat beside Winston Churchill at Yalta to plan the end of World War Two.", "In February nineteen fifty-three, Prime Minister Churchill greeted the new Queen, Elizabeth the Second, and her children.", "In May two thousand seven, on a state visit to America, the Queen toured a Washington children's hospital with Laura Bush.", "And that same month, Laura Bush posed with Elmo at a Sesame Street benefit dinner in New York.", "How is Jesus connected to Mia Khalifa?", "In fourteen eighty-two, Perugino painted Jesus handing the apostle Peter the keys of heaven, on the Sistine Chapel wall.", "Peter is counted as the first pope, and the line runs unbroken to Pope Francis in twenty thirteen.", "In twenty sixteen, Pope Francis welcomed America's Secretary of State, John Kerry, to the Vatican.", "In twenty fourteen, Kerry visited the Washington Capitals locker room to send Alex Ovechkin off to the Olympics.", "And superfan Mia Khalifa, now a sports streamer, met her hero Ovechkin and gave him a custom Capitals shirt.", "How is Kim Jong Un connected to Mickey Mouse?", "In twenty eighteen, Kim Jong Un shook hands with Donald Trump in Singapore, the first summit between their two countries.", "Back in nineteen eighty-seven, real-estate developer Donald Trump met President Ronald Reagan at a White House reception.", "And in nineteen eighty-five, after cold weather cancelled his inaugural parade, Reagan held it at Epcot, with Mickey Mouse."], "heard": [["How's", 0.0, 0.46], ["Hiller", 0.46, 0.78], ["Connected", 0.78, 1.2], ["to", 1.2, 1.28], ["Kermit", 1.28, 1.56], ["the", 1.56, 1.7], ["Frog?", 1.7, 1.9], ["In", 2.62, 2.7], ["1938,", 2.7, 3.12], ["British", 3.54, 3.64], ["Prime", 3.64, 3.8], ["Minister", 3.8, 4.12], ["Neville", 4.12, 4.34], ["Chamberlain", 4.34, 4.78], ["signed", 4.78, 5.26], ["the", 5.26, 5.44], ["Munich", 5.44, 5.6], ["Agreement", 5.6, 5.98], ["with", 5.98, 6.2], ["Hiller,", 6.2, 6.58], ["hoping", 6.68, 6.82], ["to", 6.82, 7.04], ["avoid", 7.04, 7.22], ["war.", 7.22, 7.54], ["In", 8.16, 8.22], ["1940,", 8.22, 8.66], ["Chamberlain's", 8.92, 9.4], ["fellow", 9.4, 9.54], ["conservative", 9.54, 10.02], ["Winston", 10.02, 10.24], ["Churchill", 10.24, 10.58], ["replaced", 10.58, 11.1], ["him", 11.1, 11.32], ["as", 11.32, 11.42], ["Prime", 11.42, 11.58], ["Minister.", 11.58, 11.9], ["On", 12.76, 12.8], ["victory", 12.8, 12.98], ["in", 12.98, 13.28], ["Europe", 13.28, 13.44], ["Day,", 13.44, 13.72], ["1945,", 13.86, 14.1], ["Churchill", 14.1, 14.1], ["stood", 14.1, 15.24], ["on", 15.24, 15.42], ["